From 6ffc31ab2290964b5644b8dde22ef58aff86e60f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:40:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild the site from the single-file design
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The homepage design that was signed off as one deployable HTML file is now
the whole site. Five things changed together, because they are one change:

* Every route runs on one stylesheet. globals.css is that build's stylesheet,
  ported unchanged apart from two things that differ under Next — the font
  stacks read next/font's variables, and the router's page show/hide is gone
  because each route is its own document. home.css is deleted; there is no
  longer a "homepage theme" separate from the rest of the site.

* No pill shapes. The 20px radius token is 3px, and every capsule and circle
  that survived it — eyebrow labels, hero chip, buttons and their icon
  bubbles, icon tiles, tab counts, the event series tag, the theme switch,
  the story bars, the avatar plate — is now a drawn rectangle or, where the
  shape was the only thing holding the element together, a label with a rule.

* The content boxes are gone. Three rounded cards with app icons, corner
  gradients and drop shadows is the layout every site builder emits, which is
  why it read as machine-assembled; the same three destinations are now an
  index — numbered entries, hairline rules, the figure in the margin, no
  container. The same treatment reaches the events, team, contact and
  focus-area cards: hairline frames, transparent grounds, the accent as a
  drawn bar rather than a glow. The elevation tokens resolve to none, so no
  block floats.

* Dark mode is one ground. Seven per-section tinted gradients became a single
  transparent ground plus one warmer alternate, and in dark both are the same
  black — sections are told apart by a hairline. The aurora behind them is
  roughly a third of its former strength, and the emphasis marker is an
  underline rather than an amber block that came out muddy brown over black.

* About is a section of Home. It has the same label, heading and rule as
  every other section; /about is gone and the nav points at the anchor.

The marquee ribbon is removed, and each inner page's heading no longer
appears twice.

Behaviour lives in src/lib as plain DOM modules — the cube, the reveals, the
tilt, the magnets, the story track, the theme switch — mounted by thin client
components. The cube in particular had to come across whole: its drag
rotation sits on a layer inside the perspective, which is what stops it
flattening into a turning postcard past about 40 degrees.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
